# UI and user-facing copy punctuation

In **user interface strings** and **user-facing text** (extension locales, web pages, store listing, README marketing copy, legal snippets shown to users):

- Do **not** use the em dash character `—` (U+2014).
- Use **comma** or **period** instead, whichever reads naturally in the sentence.

Applies when editing `extension/src/locales/**`, `extension/public/_locales/**`, `web/**`, and any new user-visible strings.

Internal developer docs under `docs/` should follow the same rule for consistency.

Code comments and logs: prefer comma or period over `—` as well.
